# §9 A — method/function overloading
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (additive; the non-overloaded path is byte-identical — docs/design/plano-secao9A-method-overload.md):
#   - THE GATE, keyed on `(namespace, name)`: `env_is_overloaded` / `overload_func_bindings`
#     (`src/checker/scope.tks`) count the SEALED-GLOBAL `Func` bindings sharing EXACTLY a declaring
#     namespace AND bare name. Keyed on the pair — never the bare name — so cross-namespace same-name
#     twins (`div`×3, `to_str`×3, `read`×7, …, ~40 in all) are NOT overload sets, keep their historic
#     unsuffixed symbol, and the fixpoint closes. `lookup_call_candidates` returns the whole resolving
#     set for the call site.
#   - CALL-SITE SELECTION: `select_overload` (`src/checker/typer.tks`) runs ONLY when the resolved
#     `(ns, name)` is a real overload set. Each candidate must bind by shape (`resolve_defargs` /
#     `pack_variadic_args` — parameter NAME discriminates under defaults, ruling 5) and every argument
#     must FIT its parameter (`type_value_expected` + `assignable_to`). Survivors split into an EXACT
#     tier (`type_eq`) and a WIDENED tier: an exact singleton wins outright; otherwise the highest
#     non-empty tier decides, and >1 there is a call-site ambiguity (ruling 3). A cast disambiguates
#     (ruling 4). A one-candidate set is never scored — the whole existing corpus takes that path.
#   - THE SUFFIX, one source of truth in the checker: `overload_suffix_of` (`src/checker/resolve.tks`)
#     mangles the effective signature — `"__ov"` + `_`-joined parameter-type mangle, plus a
#     `"_nm"` + parameter-name mangle ONLY when two members share identical parameter TYPES. Stamped
#     onto `TFunction.overload_suffix` (definition) and `TCall.overload_suffix` (call) in the checker,
#     "" for a sole declaration. Both backends append it verbatim after the `(ns, name)` mangle
#     (`cb_fn_name`, `src/codegen/codegen.tks`; `mangle_fn_symbol`, `src/lir/lower.tks`), so definition,
#     prototype, call and `.tsym` agree by construction and the C↔native parity holds.
#   - TAST: `overload_suffix: str` added to `TFunction` and `TCall` (`src/checker/tast.tks`), "" in
#     every existing constructor and PRESERVED across every rewrite pass (monomorph, consteval,
#     comptime-fold, the codegen lambda-lift, test-unmark) so a stamped suffix survives to codegen.
#   - NO runtime C touched. NO `.tkb` wire change (the emitted corpus spells no overload set, so
#     `overload_suffix` is "" everywhere in the compiler's own output).
